{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:47:57", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a81a1de8-6d06-430d-b25e-69f1f0dadb0c', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements-integration/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Achievements Integration",\n  "project_id": "180adf14",\n  "task_id": "1f9db6df"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01E3WBL8B8pxok27VeFxiS5D', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements-integration/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01E3WBL8B8pxok27VeFxiS5D', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Achievements System Frontend Enhancements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project**: Achievements System Frontend Enhancements\\n**Objective**: Complete the achievements system user experience by adding toast notifications, header integration, and automatic achievement tracking.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Achievement Toast Notifications & State Management\\n**Objective**: Implement toast notification system for achievement unlocks with proper state management.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `AchievementToast.jsx` component with rarity-based styling\\n- Achievement state management (context or hooks)\\n- Toast notification service integration\\n- CSS animations for toast entrance\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Toast appears within 2 seconds of achievement unlock\\n- Toast displays achievement icon, name, description\\n- Auto-dismisses after 5 seconds with manual dismissal option\\n- Clicking toast navigates to achievements dashboard\\n- Multiple toasts stack properly\\n- Rarity-based border colors implemented\\n- Dark theme compatible\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Small (primary component + state management)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Header Badge Integration & Navigation\\n**Objective**: Add achievement counter and navigation to main header with \\"NEW\\" indicator.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Updated `App.jsx` with achievements tab\\n- Achievement counter badge component\\n- \\"NEW\\" indicator logic with localStorage persistence\\n- Header navigation integration\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- \\"\\ud83c\\udfc6 Achievements\\" tab visible in header\\n- Badge shows \\"X/Y unlocked\\" format\\n- Badge highlights when new achievements exist\\n- Clicking navigates to `/achievements`\\n- Badge updates within 5 seconds of unlock\\n- \\"NEW\\" indicator clears when dashboard visited\\n- Styling matches existing header tabs\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (achievement state management)\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Small (UI integration + navigation)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Automatic Achievement Checking & Polling\\n**Objective**: Integrate automatic achievement checking into existing polling mechanism.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Achievement polling service\\n- Delta detection logic (compare previous vs current state)\\n- Integration with existing activity polling\\n- Event-based achievement checking hooks\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Achievements check automatically every polling interval\\n- New unlocks detected within one polling cycle\\n- Toast notifications trigger for new achievements\\n- Header badge updates when achievements unlock\\n- No duplicate notifications\\n- No performance impact on UI\\n- Works with existing polling system\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (toast notifications), Milestone 2 (header badge)\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Medium (polling integration + event hooks)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 4: Visual Polish & Animations\\n**Objective**: Add animations and visual enhancements for polished user experience.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- CSS animations for achievement cards\\n- \\"Newly unlocked\\" visual indicators\\n- Hover effects for achievement cards\\n- Loading states for data fetching\\n- Empty states with encouraging messages\\n- Optional confetti effect for legendary unlocks\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Achievement cards animate on first load\\n- Newly unlocked achievements have visual indicator\\n- Hover effects provide clear feedback\\n- Loading states prevent layout shift\\n- Animations enhance experience without distraction\\n- Smooth performance with 50+ achievements\\n- Respects user\'s reduced-motion preferences\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3 (complete functionality for testing animations)\\n\\n**Estimated Effort**: Small (CSS + polish)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Overall Timeline\\n- **Total Milestones**: 4\\n- **Approach**: Sequential implementation with TDD\\n- **Integration Points**: App.jsx, existing polling system, achievements dashboard\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **Risk**: Existing polling mechanism unclear\\n  - **Mitigation**: Analyze existing code structure during implementation\\n- **Risk**: Toast notification system conflicts\\n  - **Mitigation**: Use React Bootstrap Toast in isolated container\\n- **Risk**: Performance degradation from polling\\n  - **Mitigation**: Use lightweight API endpoint (getAchievementStats), implement efficient delta detection\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n1. Toast notifications appear within 2 seconds of unlock\\n2. Header badge updates in real-time\\n3. Automatic achievement checking with no user intervention\\n4. No performance degradation\\n5. Consistent dark theme across all components\\n6. Cross-browser compatibility\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n- **Framework**: React with React Bootstrap\\n- **State Management**: Context API or component state\\n- **API Integration**: Existing FastAPI backend\\n- **Styling**: CSS modules with dark theme (#1a1d29, #242836, #3a3f52)\\n- **Testing**: Component tests, integration tests, E2E tests\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LcPkrxgr791BiA6G72pBPo', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Achievements Integration', 'description': 'Frontend enhancements for achievements system, including toast notifications, header integration, and automatic achievement tracking'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LcPkrxgr791BiA6G72pBPo', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "b9d3700a", "message": "Created project: Achievements Integration", "summary": {"project_id": "b9d3700a", "project_name": "Achievements Integration", "description": "Frontend enhancements for achievements system, including toast notifications, header integration, and automatic achievement tracking", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:47:51.706759", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:47:51.706759", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:47:51.706759", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Achievements Integration\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 79.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow by sequentially coordinating with System Architect for architecture design, all three Coordinators for comprehensive task breakdown, a...\n- I successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow for this focused bug fix project. I effectively coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all Coordinators fo...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note