llaborate, maintain document history\n\n## C) System Components\n1. **Agent Creation Analysis Report**\n   - Comprehensive analysis of agent spawning patterns\n   - Includes detailed findings, statistical analysis\n   - Located at: `agent_creation_analysis_report.md`\n\n2. **Agent Type Reference Guide**\n   - Catalog of agent types\n   - Best practices for agent selection\n   - Located at: `agent_type_reference.md`\n\n3. **Verification Checklist**\n   - Step-by-step guide for correct agent spawning\n   - Pre-spawn validation criteria\n   - Located at: `verification_checklist.md`\n\n## D) File/Directory Structure\n```\n/ensemble\n└── src/\n    └── field/\n        └── ensemble_ui/\n            └── output/\n                └── agent_analysis_documentation/\n                    ├── agent_creation_analysis_report.md\n                    ├── agent_type_reference.md\n                    ├── verification_checklist.md\n                    └── architecture.md\n```\n\n## E) Data Model\n- Markdown files as primary data storage\n- Structured using headings, lists, and code blocks\n- Metadata tracked via version control\n\n## F) Deployment Strategy\n1. Manual markdown file generation\n2. Store in version-controlled repository\n3. Optional: Convert to HTML/PDF for distribution\n\n## G) Testing Strategy\n1. Manual Review Checklist\n   - Verify all requirements are met\n   - Check document completeness\n   - Validate accuracy of findings\n\n2. Version Control Validation\n   - Git commits track changes\n   - Commit messages describe updates\n\n## H) Risks and Mitigations\n1. **Risk**: Incomplete or Inaccurate Documentation\n   - **Mitigation**: Multiple reviewer passes, cross-validation with project tracking data\n\n2. **Risk**: Rapid Outdating of Documentation\n   - **Mitigation**: Regular review process, version tracking\n\n## I) Alternatives Considered\n1. Wiki-based Documentation\n   - Pros: Collaborative, easy updates\n   - Cons: Less structured, harder to version control\n   - 