{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:55:17", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-71e187bf-cb26-46db-bac9-685fff68daea', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/milestone_plan.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UDnjitUf8HjMTyRgcXC7dg', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UDnjitUf8HjMTyRgcXC7dg', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Agent Creation Analysis Documentation\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nDocument the comprehensive Agent Creation Analysis Report that identifies critical patterns of incorrect agent type assignments and task delegation errors in the ensemble system.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Core Documentation Creation (Primary)\\n**Objective**: Create the main analysis documentation and reference materials\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- `agent_creation_analysis_report.md` - Full detailed analysis report\\n- `agent_type_reference.md` - Quick reference guide for correct agent usage\\n- `verification_checklist.md` - Pre-spawn verification steps and checklists\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All three core documents are complete and saved to output directory\\n- Analysis report contains comprehensive findings and recommendations\\n- Reference guide provides actionable guidance for agent selection\\n- Checklist is practical and immediately usable\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None (standalone documentation project)\\n\\n**Timeline**: Single milestone completion\\n\\n### Project Success Definition\\n- All documentation saved to project directory: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation`\\n- Documents are complete, accurate, and actionable\\n- Reference materials support future agent creation decisions\\n\\n## Architecture Considerations\\nThis is a pure documentation project requiring:\\n- Structured markdown documentation\\n- Clear organization and formatting\\n- Comprehensive content capture\\n- Actionable reference materials\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n- Documentation-only project (no code implementation)\\n- Focus on preserving analysis findings\\n- Create reusable reference materials\\n- Ensure documents are properly formatted and organized"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QEC563tFtYDCqqF7CcgsQ2', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Creation Analysis Documentation', 'description': 'Create comprehensive documentation for agent creation analysis, including reference materials and verification checklists'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QEC563tFtYDCqqF7CcgsQ2', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "d1ded477", "message": "Created project: Agent Creation Analysis Documentation", "summary": {"project_id": "d1ded477", "project_name": "Agent Creation Analysis Documentation", "description": "Create comprehensive documentation for agent creation analysis, including reference materials and verification checklists", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:52:45.042394", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:52:45.042394", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:52:45.042394", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Creation Analysis Documentation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NRbZneKnshEirEC6PvyWL9', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'd1ded477', 'description': 'Create documentation for Agent Creation Analysis: report, reference guide, and verification checklist', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NRbZneKnshEirEC6PvyWL9', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "a535262e", "message": "Added task: Create documentation for Agent Creation Analysis: report, reference guide, and verification checklist"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V8w1yyuSXAf6C2DKd7GcVa', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/development_manager', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/milestone_plan.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation', 'project_name': 'Agent Creation Analysis Documentation', 'project_id': 'd1ded477', 'task_id': 'a535262e'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V8w1yyuSXAf6C2DKd7GcVa', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "phase": "complete", "milestones": ["Core Documentation Creation - Main analysis documentation and reference materials"], "deliverables": ["/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/agent_creation_analysis_report.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/agent_type_reference.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/agent_analysis_documentation/verification_checklist.md"], "message": "Successfully completed Agent Creation Analysis Documentation project. Created comprehensive analysis report with detailed findings and recommendations, complete agent type reference guide for proper selection, and practical verification checklist for pre-spawn validation. All documents committed to version control.", "self_analysis": "I successfully executed this documentation project by directly creating the required files when agent spawning failed. I adapted effectively to the constraint that coordinators require architecture files for documentation tasks, and delivered all three comprehensive documents as specified in the milestone plan.", "performance_analysis": "No other agents were successfully spawned for this project due to missing coordinator capabilities for pure documentation tasks. The attempt to spawn documentation_coordinator failed as expected, and frontend_coordinator failed due to missing architecture requirements, highlighting the need for specialized documentation agents in the ensemble."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KGjqShnyeXrr2QBEELU37G', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'update_task', 'project_id': 'd1ded477', 'task_id': 'a535262e', 'status': 'completed', 'note': 'Successfully created all three core documentation files: agent_creation_analysis_report.md, agent_type_reference.md, and verification_checklist.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KGjqShnyeXrr2QBEELU37G', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Updated task status to completed"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly 