s**: Display cost, duration, and model information as compact indicators\\n- **Responsive Design**: Adapt layout for different screen sizes\\n- **Professional Styling**: Consistent with existing UI theme and patterns\\n- **Data Integration**: Connect with backend metric endpoints from Milestone 1\\n\\n### 2. Utility Functions for Metric Formatting\\n- **Duration Formatting**: Convert milliseconds to appropriate units (ms/seconds/minutes)\\n- **Cost Formatting**: Display costs with $ prefix and appropriate decimal precision\\n- **Model Name Processing**: Shorten and format model names for display\\n- **Data Validation**: Handle null/undefined values gracefully\\n\\n### 3. Error Handling and Resilience\\n- **Graceful Degradation**: UI functions normally when metrics unavailable\\n- **Network Error Handling**: Manage API failures without breaking UI\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Support existing agent data without metrics\\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Enhance existing UI rather than replace\\n\\n### 4. Comprehensive Testing Suite\\n- **Unit Tests**: Test formatting functions with various input scenarios\\n- **Integration Tests**: Verify component behavior with real data\\n- **Error Scenario Testing**: Test handling of missing/invalid data\\n- **Performance Testing**: Ensure no UI rendering degradation\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend Stack\\n- **Framework**: React (existing ensemble UI stack)\\n- **Styling**: CSS modules or styled-components (consistent with existing)\\n- **Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **TypeScript**: For type safety and better development experience\\n\\n### Integration Points\\n- **Backend API**: Milestone 1 metric endpoints\\n- **Agent State**: Enhanced agent data structures with metrics\\n- **Existing Components**: AgentSummaryPane and related UI elements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\u2705 Cost estimates displayed with $ prefix and 2-4 decimal places\\n\\u2705 Duration shown in ms, seconds, or minutes based on magnitude  \\n\\u2705 Model names displayed as shortened, readable tags\\n\\u2705 UI remains compact without interface clutter\\n\\u2705 No performance impact on existing UI rendering\\n\\u2705 Graceful handling of missing/partial metric data\\n\\u2705 Consistent styling with existing UI components\\n\\u2705 Responsive design across screen sizes\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n\\u2705 Test coverage >90% for new components and utilities\\n\\u2705 No breaking changes to existing functionality\\n\\u2705 TypeScript types for all new interfaces\\n\\u2705 Documentation for component usage\\n\\u2705 Performance benchmarks within acceptable ranges\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **No Breaking Changes**: Must not disrupt existing UI functionality\\n- **Performance**: No measurable impact on UI rendering speed\\n- **Design Consistency**: Must follow existing UI patterns and themes\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Support agents without metric data\\n- **TDD Methodology**: Tests written before implementation\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Milestone 1 backend infrastructure is complete and functional\\n- API endpoints provide metric data in expected format\\n- Existing UI framework supports the required enhancements\\n- Development environment has necessary testing tools configured\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Major UI redesign or layout changes\\n- Real-time metric updates (use existing refresh patterns)\\n- Advanced analytics or trend visualization\\n- Export functionality for metric data\\n- Mobile-specific optimizations beyond responsive design\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\nFollowing TDD methodology:\\n1. **Write Tests First**: Create comprehensive test suite for all features\\n2. **Implement Incrementally**: Build features to pass tests one by one\\n3. **Refactor**: Optimize and clean code while maintaining test coverage\\n4. **Integration**: Ensure seamless integration with existing UI components\\n\\nThis approach ensures high quality, maintainable code that meets all requirements while minimizing risk of introducing bugs or breaking existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XmEF2dV6NbgCTU2DYy62MW', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement Milestone 2', 'description': 'Implement frontend metrics display for agent execution tracking with enhanced user experience and data visualization'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XmEF2dV6NbgCTU2DYy62MW', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "5a2e3b18", "message": "Created project: Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement Milestone 2", "summary": {"project_id": "5a2e3b18", "project_name": "Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement Milestone 2", "description": "Implement frontend metrics display for agent execution tracking with enhanced user experience and data visualization", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:53:10.273641", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:53:10.273641", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:53:10.273641", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Cost Tracking Enhancement Milestone 2\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01T7JbQhEiVFo5uRJG6u1n2b', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01T7JbQhEiVFo5uRJG6u1n2b', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014GR4RcjrwMq9UbqAaTmWhr', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014GR4RcjrwMq9UbqAaTmWhr', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "completed", "response_type": "conversational", "message": "Now I\'ll analyze the requirements and create a comprehensive architecture proposal. This is an interesting project focused on enhancing an existing activity tracking system while maintaining backward compatibility.", "agent": "System Architect"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GTiu9BU7ECNRKExqscTNY7', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GTiu9BU7ECNRKExqscTNY7', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Activity Tracking Fixes - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfd7\\ufe0f Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Decorator/Wrapper with Contextual Tracking\\n\\nThe proposed architecture implements a lightweight, non-intrusive activity tracking system using a decorator/wrapper pattern that allows optional context propagation without disrupting existing functionality.\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udd27 Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Primary Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Existing Infrastructure**: Leveraging current project utilities\\n- **Design Pattern**: Decorator/Wrapper with Context Propagation\\n\\n### Key Design Principles\\n- Minimal Overhead\\n- Optional Tracking\\n- Backward Compatibility\\n- Graceful Degradation\\n\\n## \\ud83e\\udde9 System Components\\n\\n### 1. Enhanced WriteFileTool\\n- Wrapper around existing file writing mechanism\\n- Optional tracking context parameters\\n- Preserves original functionality\\n- Low-overhead tracking integration\\n\\n### 2. ActivityTracker\\n- Centralized tracking mechanism\\n- Supports context-aware logging\\n- Increments request counts\\n- Maintains audit trail\\n\\n### 3. Context Propagation Mechanism\\n- Lightweight context object\\n- Supports optional tracking details\\n- Zero-overhead when not in use\\n- Consistent across tools\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udcc2 Proposed Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/runtime/agents/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tools.py           # Enhanced WriteFileTool\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 activity_tracker.py # Enhanced ActivityTracker\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 context.py         # Context propagation utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py\\n```\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udd04 Data Flow Diagram\\n```\\n[Agent Context] -> [WriteFileTool] -> [ActivityTracker]\\n    \\u2193                   \\u2193                  \\u2193\\nOptional Context    File Operation     Event Logging\\n```\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udee1\\ufe0f Enhanced WriteFileTool Implementation\\n```python\\nclass WriteFileTool:\\n    def __init__(self, agent_id=None, agent_name=None, request_id=None):\\n        self.tracking_context = {\\n            \'agent_id\': agent_id,\\n            \'agent_name\': agent_name,\\n            \'request_id\': request_id\\n        } if any([agent_id, agent_name, request_id]) else None\\n\\n    def execute(self, file_path, content):\\n        # Original file writing logic\\n        result = original_write_file(file_path, content)\\n\\n        # Optional tracking (minimal overhead)\\n        if self.tracking_context:\\n            ActivityTracker.record_file_event(\\n                file_path=file_path,\\n                context=self.tracking_context\\n            )\\n\\n        return result\\n```\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udea6 Tracking Context Mechanism\\n- Completely optional\\n- Passes through existing tool interfaces\\n- Zero-configuration default behavior\\n- Flexible opt-in tracking\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udd2c Performance Considerations\\n- Tracking adds < 1ms per operation\\n- Memory overhead < 1MB\\n- No performance impact when tracking disabled\\n- Graceful degradation on tracking failures\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udee1\\ufe0f Reliability Strategy\\n- File operations always succeed\\n- Tracking failures don\'t interrupt core functionality\\n- No exceptions propagated from tracking subsystem\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udd0d Alternative Approaches Considered\\n\\n### 1. Global Tracking\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Less flexible, potential performance overhead\\n- **Decision**: Rejected in favor of optional context\\n\\n### 2. Separate Tracking Service\\n- **Pros**: Centralized tracking\\n- **Cons**: Additional infrastructure complexity\\n- **Decision**: Rejected; current approach more lightweight\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udea7 Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Performance Risks\\n- **Risk**: Tracking might slow file operations\\n- **Mitigation**: Ultra-lightweight implementation, optional tracking\\n\\n### Integration Risks\\n- **Risk**: Breaking existing functionality\\n- **Mitigation**: Comprehensive testing, backward compatibility\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfaf Success Criteria\\n- 90%+ Test Coverage\\n- Zero Breaking Changes\\n- < 1ms Tracking Overhead\\n- Graceful Optional Tracking\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udd2e Future Considerations\\n- Real-time monitoring dashboards\\n- Enhanced tracking metrics\\n- External system integrations\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udccb Open Questions for Stakeholder Review\\n1. Acceptable tracking context parameters?\\n2. Logging verbosity preferences?\\n3. Any specific audit trail requirements?\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfc1 Recommended Next Steps\\n1. Implement core tracking mechanism\\n2. Develop comprehensive unit tests\\n3. Integration testing\\n4. Documentation updates"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UgJ5sKBRDujs8EASx97xdm', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Enhance frontend metrics display for agent execution tracking', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UgJ5sKBRDujs8EASx97xdm', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 12, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "dependencies": ["API Client Enhancement \\u2192 Agent Metrics Dashboard Component", "API Client Enhancement \\u2192 File Generation Activity List", "API Client Enhancement \\u2192 Agent Performance Metrics Cards", "API Client Enhancement \\u2192 Activity Timeline Visualization", "API Client Enhancement \\u2192 Tracking Configuration Panel", "API Client Enhancement \\u2192 Metrics Export Service", "Agent Metrics Dashboard Component \\u2192 Real-time Metrics WebSocket Integration", "File Generation Activity List \\u2192 Activity Search and Filter Component", "Agent Performance Metrics Cards \\u2192 Metrics Comparison Tool"], "message": "Successfully identified 12 frontend tasks for enhancing metrics display. Tasks are organized into 4 phases: Core Metrics Display (4 tasks), Detailed Views (3 tasks), Advanced Features (3 tasks), and Real-time and Comparison (2 tasks). All tasks focus on